## 1. Vault::lock Reentrancy Scenario
Within `Vault::lock`, there is a potential reentrancy scenario. It is possible for the locker to execute a re-entrant call on `lock`, thus enabling the vault to become unlocked in the middle of the first lock process. Currently, there is no impact, but it would be appropriate to ensure that the lock is in an unlocked state before calling `lock`.

```solidity
// pancake-v4-core/src/pool-bin/libraries/BinPool.sol
function lock(bytes calldata data) external override returns (bytes memory result) {
    /// @dev only one locker at a time
    SettlementGuard.setLocker(msg.sender);
